UL 1598 6.14.2.2 ('same location as the power supply connection means') and 6.16.3(a) (an insulated grounding conductor counted in the compartment) both point to a green screw inside the enclosure, which also removes the routing problem. The reviewer weighs the opening against 11.4.4; the clause that names openings through a supporting plate is 11.5.3 (see missed).

